---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { n, fmtDate } from '../../lib/reports';
import fs from 'node:fs';
import path from 'node:path';

const dir = path.resolve(process.cwd(), 'public/data/avm');
const meta = fs.existsSync(path.join(dir, 'meta.json')) ? JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(path.join(dir, 'meta.json'), 'utf8')) : null;
const acc = meta?.accuracy;
---
<Base title="What is it worth — valuation from registered prices" crumbs={[{ label: 'Valuation' }]}>
  <div class="avm">
    <h1>What is it worth</h1>
    <p class="lede">A valuation built from what buyers actually paid at the land registry — not from what anyone is asking. Pick the tower, the bedroom count and the size. {meta && <>Registered sales to {fmtDate(meta.asOf)}, {n(meta.cells)} tower-and-bedroom combinations across {n(meta.buildings)} buildings.</>} General information from the public record, not a formal valuation and not investment advice.</p>

    {acc && <div class="acc">
      <div><b>How often it is right.</b> Measured, not claimed: the model is tested against {n(acc.testedOn)} registered sales it was never trained on, held out from {fmtDate(acc.heldOutFrom)}. These figures are recomputed every time the data refreshes.</div>
      <div class="accrow">
        <div class="kpi"><div class="v">{acc.medianAbsErrorPct}%</div><div class="l">Median error — half of valuations are closer than this</div></div>
        <div class="kpi"><div class="v">{acc.within10Pct}%</div><div class="l">Within 10% of the registered price</div></div>
        <div class="kpi"><div class="v">{acc.within20Pct}%</div><div class="l">Within 20%</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>}

    <div class="picker">
      <label class="fld"><span>Tower or building</span>
        <input id="q" type="text" autocomplete="off" placeholder="start typing — e.g. Binghatti" />
        <div id="sugg" class="sugg" hidden></div>
      </label>
      <label class="fld sm"><span>Bedrooms</span><select id="rm"></select></label>
      <label class="fld sm"><span>Size, sq m</span><input id="sz" type="number" min="15" step="1" /></label>
    </div>

    <div id="out"></div>

    <section class="qs">
      <h2><span class="no">1</span>How it works</h2>
      <p class="why">{meta?.method}</p>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li><b>Find the evidence.</b> Every sale registered in that same tower, same bedroom count, within a quarter of the size, over the last twelve months.</li>
        <li><b>Bring it to today.</b> A sale from March was struck in a different market, so each comparable is carried forward on its own area's monthly price index.</li>
        <li><b>Correct for size.</b> Price per square metre falls as units get larger — measured across thousands of towers at {meta?.sizeElasticity}, so a unit 10% bigger trades about {meta ? (((1.1 ** meta.sizeElasticity) - 1) * 100).toFixed(1) : '−3.2'}% lower per square metre. Each comparable is moved onto the subject's size along that curve.</li>
        <li><b>Take the middle.</b> The median of the adjusted comparables, times the size.</li>
        <li><b>Say how sure we are.</b> The range is not the spread of the comparables — that would have contained the true price only 4 times in 10. It is the 10th to 90th percentile of the model's <em>own measured error</em> on sales it had never seen, which is why we can say eight in ten land inside it.</li>
      </ol>
      <h2><span class="no">2</span>When we show nothing</h2>
      <p class="why">A tower with fewer than {meta?.minComps ?? 5} registered sales of that bedroom count in twelve months gets no valuation. Not a wide one — none. We also do not publish area-level averages as a fallback, though we compute them: they came out at roughly twice the error of the tower-level figure, and a number that is twice as wrong does not become acceptable by being the only one available.</p>
      {acc && <div class="scroll"><table>
        <thead><tr><th>Comparable sales available</th><th class="num">Tested on</th><th class="num">Median error</th><th class="num">Within 10%</th><th>Published range</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>{acc.byCompCount.map((c: any) => <tr>
          <td>{c.comps}</td><td class="num">{n(c.n)}</td>
          <td class="num">{c.medianAbsErrorPct?.toFixed(2)}%</td>
          <td class="num">{c.within10Pct?.toFixed(1)}%</td>
          <td>−{Math.round((1 - c.lowMult) * 100)}% to +{Math.round((c.highMult - 1) * 100)}%</td>
        </tr>)}</tbody>
      </table></div>}
      <p class="reads"><b>What this shows.</b> That the model is more accurate where the evidence is denser, which is what you would expect and what we would want you to check. <b>How to read it.</b> The published range widens as the evidence thins, so a valuation on five comparables carries a visibly wider band than one on fifty. What the register cannot tell us is floor, view and finish — so a high floor with a view will sit above our range and a ground-floor unit facing a wall below it. That is the ceiling on any valuation built from transaction records alone, ours included.</p>
    </section>
  </div>

  <script is:inline>
    (function () {
      var cells = null, byB = {}, names = [], cur = null, meta = null;
      var q = document.getElementById('q'), rm = document.getElementById('rm'),
          sz = document.getElementById('sz'), out = document.getElementById('out'),
          sugg = document.getElementById('sugg');

      Promise.all([
        fetch('/data/avm/cells.json').then(function (r) { return r.json(); }),
        fetch('/data/avm/meta.json').then(function (r) { return r.json(); })
      ]).then(function (res) {
        cells = res[0]; meta = res[1];
        cells.forEach(function (c) { (byB[c.building] = byB[c.building] || []).push(c); });
        names = Object.keys(byB).sort();
        var p = new URLSearchParams(location.search).get('b');
        if (p && byB[p]) { q.value = p; pick(p); }
      });

      function esc(s) { return String(s).replace(/[&<>"]/g, function (c) { return ({ '&': '&amp;', '<': '&lt;', '>': '&gt;', '"': '&quot;' })[c]; }); }
      var f0 = function (v) { return Math.round(v).toLocaleString('en-GB'); };

      q.addEventListener('input', function () {
        var t = q.value.trim().toLowerCase();
        if (t.length < 2) { sugg.hidden = true; return; }
        var hit = names.filter(function (x) { return x.toLowerCase().indexOf(t) >= 0; }).slice(0, 12);
        sugg.innerHTML = hit.map(function (x) { return '<button type="button" data-b="' + esc(x) + '">' + esc(x) + '</button>'; }).join('');
        sugg.hidden = !hit.length;
      });
      sugg.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
        var b = e.target.getAttribute('data-b');
        if (!b) return;
        q.value = b; sugg.hidden = true; pick(b);
      });
      document.addEventListener('click', function (e) { if (!sugg.contains(e.target) && e.target !== q) sugg.hidden = true; });

      function pick(b) {
        cur = byB[b];
        rm.innerHTML = cur.map(function (c) { return '<option value="' + esc(c.rooms) + '">' + esc(c.rooms) + '</option>'; }).join('');
        sz.value = cur[0].typicalSizeSqm;
        render();
      }
      rm.addEventListener('change', function () {
        var c = cur.filter(function (x) { return x.rooms === rm.value; })[0];
        if (c) sz.value = c.typicalSizeSqm;
        render();
      });
      sz.addEventListener('input', render);

      function render() {
        if (!cur) return;
        var c = cur.filter(function (x) { return x.rooms === rm.value; })[0] || cur[0];
        var size = parseFloat(sz.value);
        if (!size || size <= 0) { out.innerHTML = ''; return; }
        // the same size curve the engine uses, so the page and the model never disagree
        var psm = c.aedPerSqm * Math.pow(size / c.typicalSizeSqm, meta.sizeElasticity);
        var v = psm * size;
        var lo = v * c.bandLow, hi = v * c.bandHigh;
        var far = Math.abs(Math.log(size / c.typicalSizeSqm)) > Math.log(1.33);
        out.innerHTML =
          '<div class="result">' +
            '<div class="hdr">' + esc(c.building) + ' · ' + esc(c.rooms) + ' · ' + f0(size) + ' sq m</div>' +
            '<div class="big">AED ' + f0(v) + '</div>' +
            '<div class="band">Eight in ten sales like this landed between <b>AED ' + f0(lo) + '</b> and <b>AED ' + f0(hi) + '</b></div>' +
            '<dl>' +
              '<div><dt>Evidence</dt><dd>' + c.comps + ' registered sales in this tower, last 12 months</dd></div>' +
              '<div><dt>Confidence</dt><dd><span class="chip ' + (c.confidence === 'high' ? 'ok' : c.confidence === 'medium' ? 'warn' : 'muted') + '">' + c.confidence + '</span></dd></div>' +
              '<div><dt>Implied per sq m</dt><dd>AED ' + f0(psm) + '</dd></div>' +
              '<div><dt>Most recent sale</dt><dd>' + esc(c.lastSale) + '</dd></div>' +
              '<div><dt>Typical size here</dt><dd>' + c.typicalSizeSqm + ' sq m</dd></div>' +
              '<div><dt>Off-plan share of comparables</dt><dd>' + c.offplanShare + '%</dd></div>' +
            '</dl>' +
            (far ? '<p class="warn-note">The size you entered is well outside the range of units that actually traded here (' + c.typicalSizeSqm + ' sq m typical). The size curve is being extrapolated, so treat this as indicative only.</p>' : '') +
            '<p class="foot">Floor, view and finish are not in the land registry, so a high floor with a view will sit above this range and a low floor facing a wall below it.</p>' +
          '</div>';
      }
    })();
  </script>

  <style is:global>
    .avm .acc{border:1px solid var(--border);border-left:4px solid var(--accent);border-radius:12px;background:var(--surface);padding:15px 18px;margin:14px 0 20px;font-size:13.5px}
    .avm .accrow{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(150px,1fr));gap:10px;margin-top:12px}
    .avm .kpi{background:var(--wash);border-radius:9px;padding:10px 12px}
    .avm .kpi .v{font-family:var(--serif);font-size:23px;font-weight:650}
    .avm .kpi .l{font-size:11.5px;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.35;margin-top:2px}
    .avm .picker{display:flex;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:flex-end;margin:0 0 18px}
    .avm .fld{position:relative;flex:1 1 320px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:5px}
    .avm .fld.sm{flex:0 1 150px}
    .avm .fld span{font-size:11.5px;color:var(--muted);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.05em}
    .avm input,.avm select{font:inherit;font-size:15px;padding:10px 12px;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:9px;background:var(--surface);color:var(--ink);width:100%}
    .avm input:focus,.avm select:focus{outline:2px solid var(--accent);outline-offset:-1px}
    .avm .sugg{position:absolute;top:100%;left:0;right:0;z-index:20;background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:9px;margin-top:4px;max-height:280px;overflow:auto;box-shadow:0 8px 24px rgba(0,0,0,.09)}
    .avm .sugg button{display:block;width:100%;text-align:left;background:none;border:0;font:inherit;font-size:14px;padding:9px 12px;cursor:pointer;color:var(--ink)}
    .avm .sugg button:hover{background:var(--wash)}
    .avm .result{border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:12px;background:var(--surface);padding:20px 22px;margin:0 0 22px}
    .avm .result .hdr{font-size:13px;color:var(--muted)}
    .avm .result .big{font-family:var(--serif);font-size:40px;font-weight:650;letter-spacing:-.02em;margin:4px 0 2px}
    .avm .result .band{font-size:14px;color:var(--ink2)}
    .avm .result dl{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(180px,1fr));gap:10px 18px;margin:16px 0 0;padding-top:14px;border-top:1px solid var(--grid)}
    .avm .result dt{font-size:11px;color:var(--muted);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.05em}
    .avm .result dd{margin:2px 0 0;font-size:14px}
    .avm .result .foot{font-size:12.5px;color:var(--muted);margin:14px 0 0;padding-top:10px;border-top:1px solid var(--grid)}
    .avm .result .warn-note{font-size:12.5px;color:#7a5f22;background:rgba(169,133,62,.1);border-radius:8px;padding:9px 11px;margin:12px 0 0}
    .avm .steps{font-size:14px;line-height:1.65;padding-left:20px;max-width:820px}
    .avm .steps li{margin-bottom:7px}
  </style>
</Base>
